            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for to run out, then the Tamil for to wear down."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: உரிமம்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "உரிமம் — urimam — \"a licence; a permit\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ஓட்டுநர் உரிமம் இல்லாமல் கார் ஓட்டக் கூடாது. ōṭṭunar urimam illāmal kār ōṭṭak kūṭātu. You must not drive a car without a driving licence."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ஓட்டுநர் உரிமம் (urimam) is a driving licence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "உரிமம் (urimam) is native Dravidian, a modern coinage built on the root of உரிமை, \"a right, ownership\" (DEDR 654), with the noun ending -am in place of -mai: a right given on paper."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
